// Devanagari Hindi commands (12 cases).
//
// This stratum exists for two things English cannot exercise:
//
// 1. SCRIPT HANDLING. Devanagari writes its vowels and virama as COMBINING
//    MARKS, which is what made the client gate's original tokenizer silently
//    erase every Hindi phrase (found and fixed at M6). NFKC also decomposes
//    nukta letters. Any regression in that handling shows up here first.
//
// 2. THE LANGUAGE TRAP. `language` is set ONLY from an explicit request and is
//    never inferred from the script the teacher typed in — a Hinglish or Hindi
//    request very often wants an English-medium printed paper. Every case below
//    that does not name a language carries `language` in `notStated`, and any
//    violation is a HARD GATE failure, not a percentage point.
//
// cmd.hi.008 is the sharpest form of the trap: the word "हिंदी" appears as the
// SUBJECT. Setting `language: hi` from it is exactly the mistake the structural
// design at M4 exists to prevent.

